~pages/Addons/aboutAddons.html
About add-ons
Learn about types and sources of add-on for Affinity.
~pages/Addons/exportingAddons.html
Exporting add-ons
Export custom content so you can import and use it in Affinity on other devices.
~pages/Addons/importingAddons.html
Importing add-ons
Import custom content from add-on files you have created or received from a third party.
~pages/Addons/linkingContent.html
Linking custom content across apps
Make custom content you have created or imported available in all your Affinity apps.
~pages/Adjustments/adjustment_3dLut.html
LUT adjustment
The LUT adjustment allows you to emulate image colours used in a variety of media platforms.
~pages/Adjustments/adjustment_HSL.html
HSL adjustment
Fine-tune, or completely change, colours by modifying the hue, staturation and luminosity.
~pages/Adjustments/adjustment_applying.html
Applying adjustments
Apply adjustments to your design for creative or corrective purposes.
~pages/Adjustments/adjustment_blackAndWhite.html
Black and White adjustment
Convert a colour image to monochrome while maintaining full control over how individual colours are converted.
~pages/Adjustments/adjustment_brightnessContrast.html
Brightness / Contrast adjustment
Adjust the values in the shadows and highlights, and the overall tonal range, of images.
~pages/Adjustments/adjustment_channelMixer.html
Channel Mixer adjustment
Adjust the colour of individual channels to produce effects not easily achieved with other colour adjustment tools.
~pages/Adjustments/adjustment_clrBalance.html
Colour Balance adjustment
The Colour Balance adjustment provides a way to modify the contribution of particular colours to a set tonal range.
~pages/Adjustments/adjustment_curves.html
Curves adjustment
Adjust the colour and tone of images using curves.
~pages/Adjustments/adjustment_exposure.html
Exposure adjustment
Correct highlight and shadow detail.
~pages/Adjustments/adjustment_gradientMap.html
Gradient map adjustment
The Gradient Map adjustment maps the greyscale tonal range of an image to a specified colour gradient.
~pages/Adjustments/adjustment_invert.html
Invert adjustment
Create a negative image by inverting all colour channels.
~pages/Adjustments/adjustment_lensfilter.html
Lens Filter adjustment
Emulate the look of a tonal lens filter.
~pages/Adjustments/adjustment_levels.html
Levels adjustment
Adjust the tonal values of an image by setting the black point, white point, and gamma.
~pages/Adjustments/adjustment_normals.html
Normals adjustment
Edit lighting layers (normal maps) from 3D game art apps
~pages/Adjustments/adjustment_ocio.html
OpenColorIO adjustment
The OCIO adjustment performs colour transforms to help with a colour managed workflow.
~pages/Adjustments/adjustment_posterize.html
Posterise adjustment
Create large, flat areas of colour or tone in your images using the Posterise adjustment.
~pages/Adjustments/adjustment_reclr.html
Recolour adjustment
Create a monochrome image using the full spectrum of colours using a Recolour adjustment.
~pages/Adjustments/adjustment_selectiveClr.html
Selective Colour adjustment
The Selective Colour adjustment provides a way to subtly adjust and enhance colours in your image on an individual channel basis.
~pages/Adjustments/adjustment_shadowsHighlights.html
Shadows / Highlights adjustment
Adjust the lightness of the shadows and highlights in your image using the Shadows/Highlights adjustment.
~pages/Adjustments/adjustment_softProof.html
Soft Proof adjustment
Preview the effect of creating an output for a specific colour space or device.
~pages/Adjustments/adjustment_splitToning.html
Split Toning adjustment
Adjusts the tonal and colour values of pixels in an image.
~pages/Adjustments/adjustment_threshold.html
Threshold adjustment
Create two-tone, black and white images using the Threshold adjustment.
~pages/Adjustments/adjustment_vibrance.html
Vibrance adjustment
Adjust the intensity of subtle colours in your images while minimising the over-saturation of more intense colours.
~pages/Adjustments/adjustment_whiteBalance.html
White Balance adjustment
Remove unwanted colour casts, or make your design warmer or cooler, using the White Balance adjustment.
