Design aids and artboards
Discussion of using design aids with artboards.
~pages/Artboards/artboards_export.html
Exporting artboards
Discussion of exporting artboards and documents with artboards.
~pages/Artboards/artboards_moveResize.html
Selecting, moving and resizing artboards
Discussion of selecting, moving and resizing artboards.
~pages/Artboards/artboards_objectControl.html
Moving artboard content
Move objects between artboards using Edit All Layers.
~pages/Artboards/artboards_print.html
Printing artboards
Discussion of printing artboards and documents with artboards.
~pages/Artboards/artboards_renameView.html
Renaming and viewing artboards
Discussion of renaming and viewing artboards.
~pages/Clr/ClrModels.html
Colour models
Find out how to choose a colour model
~pages/Clr/ClrProfiles.html
Colour management
Set up colour profiles for colour management.
~pages/Clr/aboutClr.html
About colour
An introduction to colour use in Affinity Designer.
~pages/Clr/aboutClrSpaces.html
About colour spaces
Find out how a colour space defines the colours available to the current colour model.
~pages/Clr/clrChords.html
Colour chords
Learn how to create and store colour spreads using professional colour theory.
~pages/Clr/globalClr.html
Global colours
Automatically update fill and stroke colours across multiple objects using global colours.
~pages/Clr/gradientEditor.html
Gradient and bitmap fills
Apply colour gradients and bitmaps to fills and strokes.
~pages/Clr/ocio.html
Using OpenColorIO
Use OCIO for colour managed workflows.
~pages/Clr/overprint.html
Overprinting
Make colours overprint for professional printing.
~pages/Clr/samplingClr.html
Sampling colours
Pick up colours from objects on your page or pixels on your screen.
~pages/Clr/selectingClr.html
Selecting colours
There are various ways to select and apply colour in Affinity apps.
~pages/Clr/spotClr.html
Spot colours
Convert a standard colour to a spot colour for professional printing.
~pages/Clr/transparency.html
Transparency
Find out about transparency and how it is applied to your design.
~pages/Clr/transparencyEditor.html
Transparency editing
The Transparency Editor dialog lets you customise transparency gradients for object fills and strokes.
~pages/CurvesShapes/about_geometricShapes.html
About geometric shapes
Geometric and other special shapes can be easily created using one of the corresponding shape tools.
~pages/CurvesShapes/about_linesAndShapes.html
About lines, curves and shapes
Open curves and closed shapes can be created and are controlled by nodes and control handles.
~pages/CurvesShapes/contouringShapes.html
Contouring curves and shapes
Contouring lets you offset the outline and stroke of a curve or shape.
~pages/CurvesShapes/corneringShapes.html
Cornering shapes
The Corner Tool rounds sharp corners on any closed shape.
~pages/CurvesShapes/draw_geometricShapes.html
Draw and edit shapes
Geometric and other special shapes can be easily created and edited with precision and speed.
~pages/CurvesShapes/draw_linesAndShapes.html
Draw curves and shapes
You can use the Pen Tool to create curves and shapes.
~pages/CurvesShapes/draw_pencilLines.html
Drawing pencil lines
Use the Pencil Tool to apply pencil lines, giving a hand-drawn effect to your design.
~pages/CurvesShapes/edit_linesAndShapes.html
Edit curves and shapes
Edit your curve by changing curvature, add and delete nodes, join and split curves.
~pages/CurvesShapes/expandStroke.html
Expand stroke
Expand stroke expands the stroke of a shape or line, converting the line's boundaries into paths forming a closed shape.
~pages/CurvesShapes/fillMode.html
Fill modes
Shapes which have been constructed using self-intersecting lines can be filled in two different ways.
~pages/CurvesShapes/multiStrokesAndFills.html
Using multiple strokes and fills
Multiple strokes and fills can be applied to any selected object to produce striking complex visual effects.
~pages/CurvesShapes/pressure.html
Pressure sensitivity
Use a pen tablet, Force Touch device or simulated pressure via mouse for pressure-sensitive line and brush work
~pages/CurvesShapes/select_align_nodes.html
Selecting and aligning nodes
Select and align a curve's or shape's nodes.
~pages/CurvesShapes/transform_linesAndShapes.html
Transforming curves and shapes
Lines and shapes can be transformed via node manipulation.
~pages/DesignAids/clipToCanvas.html
Clip to Canvas
Clip to Canvas hides all objects on the pasteboard.
~pages/DesignAids/constraints.html
Constraints
Use constraints to control scaling and anchoring of a child object when scaling their parent object.
~pages/DesignAids/constructionSnapping.html
Construction snapping for curves
For curve drawing, snap a node's control handle to various angles and alignments.
~pages/DesignAids/curveSnapping.html
Curve snapping
Use curve snapping to align nodes and control handles.
~pages/DesignAids/dynamicGuides.html
Dynamic guides
Dynamic guides are automated, temporary guides which appear to help with your image composition.
~pages/DesignAids/grids.html
Grids
A non-printing, non-exporting grid can be displayed on top of your image in order to help you to lay out objects accurately.
~pages/DesignAids/grids_axonometric.html
Isometric and axonometric grids
Create 2.5D parallel projections using projection grids.
~pages/DesignAids/guides.html
Ruler and column guides
Guides are non-printing, non-exporting lines that float over the page and assist with positioning objects.
~pages/DesignAids/margins.html
Margins
Page margins allow you to design with printing in mind.
~pages/DesignAids/measuring.html
Measuring
Measuring lets you display the distance between objects, plus the area and perimeter length of objects.
~pages/DesignAids/pixelAlign.html
Force Pixel Alignment
Force Pixel Alignment snaps to full pixels when objects are created, moved or modified.
~pages/DesignAids/rotateCanvas.html
Rotate document view
Rotate your document view for temporary orientation control.
~pages/DesignAids/rulers.html
Rulers
Rulers are useful when you need to accurately place objects or guides in the document view.
~pages/DesignAids/snapping.html
Snapping
Snapping simplifies placing, creating and aligning objects without the need to set up rulers or guides.
~pages/DesignAids/snapshot.html
Using snapshots
Use snapshots to 'freeze frame' stages in your design progress to fall back to.
~pages/DesignAids/undo.html
Using undo, redo and history
Rolls back/forward to operations made during session.
~pages/ExportPersona/exportOptionsPanel.html
Export Options panel
Apply export options to export areas defined in Export Persona.
~pages/ExportPersona/exportPersona.html
Exporting using Export Persona
Export your document to a universally recognised raster image format.
~pages/ExportPersona/exportPersona_layersPanel.html
Layers panel (Export Persona)
The Layers panel in Export Persona lets you create slices from layers, groups, or objects.
~pages/ExportPersona/exportSettings.html
Export Settings
Learn about the export settings available in the Export dialog and Export Options panel.
~pages/ExportPersona/slicesPanel.html
Slices panel
Export designs to universally recognised image formats using the Slices panel.
~pages/Extras/hardwareAcceleration.html
Hardware acceleration
Boosting performance by processing on your device's GPU instead of its CPU.
~pages/Extras/penTablet.html
Using pen tablets
Use a pen tablet for a natural drawing experience.
~pages/Extras/sidecar.html
Using Sidecar with your Affinity Mac app
Apple's Sidecar functionality in macOS and iPadOS lets you combine the benefits of your iPad’s touchscreen and Apple Pencil with your Mac.
~pages/Extras/surfaceDial.html
Using Surface Dial with your Affinity Windows apps
Microsoft's Surface Dial can provide fast access to the Affinity commands and controls you need the most.
~pages/Extras/surfacePen.html
Using Surface Pen with your Affinity Windows apps
Microsoft's Surface Pen enables you to draw and paint with precision directly on your Surface device's display.
~pages/Extras/trackpads.html
Using a trackpad
Use gestures to enhance your workflow
~pages/Filters/filter_meshWarp.html
Mesh Warp
The Mesh Warp filter allows you to manipulate a flexible mesh grid to warp an image or a vector shape.
~pages/Filters/filter_perspective.html
Live Perspective filter
The Perspective filter can be used to either correct perspective caused by lens distortion, or to apply perspective for a creative effect.
~pages/GetStarted/DocumentSetup.html
Document setup
Change your document setup (e.g., page size) at any time.
~pages/GetStarted/NewDocument.html
Create new documents
Create a new document including setting up colour settings and page dimensions.
~pages/GetStarted/NewFromClipboard.html
New from clipboard
Create a new document based on the clipboard contents.
~pages/GetStarted/aboutBitDepth.html
About bit depth
A brief look at the different bit depths.
~pages/GetStarted/close.html
Close
Close one or more documents once you've finished your session or completed your design.
~pages/GetStarted/documentUnits.html
Document units
Find out how to set and modify your document units.
~pages/GetStarted/drawingScale.html
Drawing scale
Apply a drawing scale to open documents.
~pages/GetStarted/editInOtherAffinityApps.html
Editing files in other Affinity apps
Editing project files in their own native apps allows layout, graphic design and photography work to be developed independently of other disciplines.
~pages/GetStarted/importAdobe.html
Importing Adobe documents
Importing Adobe documents.
~pages/GetStarted/importCAD.html
Importing CAD documents
Importing CAD documents.
~pages/GetStarted/importPDF.html
Importing PDF documents
Importing PDF documents.
~pages/GetStarted/openDocument.html
Open documents and images
Open previously saved documents, photos and images.
~pages/GetStarted/pan.html
Pan/Scroll the document view
Move around your zoomed-in document by panning
~pages/GetStarted/registerAndSync.html
App activation and installing content
Activate your Affinity app and install content purchased from the Affinity Store.
~pages/GetStarted/save.html
Save
Save your design project file to protect changes and store for later editing.
~pages/GetStarted/templates.html
Document templates
Document templates contain reusable content such as text styles, graphics and layouts.
~pages/GetStarted/view.html
Viewing
Different viewing options allow you maximum flexibility when creating your designs.
~pages/GetStarted/zoom.html
Zooming
Work on specfic areas of your drawing by zooming
~pages/Introduction/about_Personas.html
Personas
An introduction to Personas.
~pages/Introduction/about_designer.html
Affinity Designer 2
An introduction to Affinity Designer
~pages/Introduction/keyFeatures.html
Features
An overview of Affinity Designer key features.
~pages/Introduction/switchingPersonas.html
Switching Personas
Switching Personas gives you access to tools unique to that Persona.
~pages/LayerFX/create_layerFX.html
Using layer effects
Effects can be applied to objects via the Quick FX panel or dialog.
~pages/LayerFX/layerFX_3D.html
3D Effect
The 3D effect is used to create the impression of a textured surface.
~pages/LayerFX/layerFX_bevelEmboss.html
Bevel/Emboss
The Bevel/Emboss effect is used to add rounded-edges and shadows to give a 3D impression.
~pages/LayerFX/layerFX_clrOverlay.html
Colour Overlay
The Colour Overlay effect is used to apply a solid colour on top of any existing colours.
~pages/LayerFX/layerFX_gaussianBlur.html
Gaussian Blur
The Gaussian Blur effect is used to create a pleasing, smooth blur using a weighted average.
~pages/LayerFX/layerFX_gradientOverlay.html
Gradient Overlay
The Gradient Overlay effect is used to apply a colour gradient on top of any existing colours.
~pages/LayerFX/layerFX_innerGlow.html
Inner Glow
The Inner Glow effect is used to add a colour border to the inside of an object.
~pages/LayerFX/layerFX_innerShadow.html
Inner Shadow
The Inner Shadow effect is used to add a diffused shadow to the inside of an object.
~pages/LayerFX/layerFX_outerGlow.html
Outer Glow
The Outer Glow effect is used to add a colour border to edges.
~pages/LayerFX/layerFX_outerShadow.html
Outer Shadow
The Outer Shadow effect is used to add a shadow to edges.
~pages/LayerFX/layerFX_outline.html
Outline
The Outline effect is used to add a coloured outline.
~pages/Layers/LayerMasks.html
Layer masking
Layer masks allow you to selectively hide layer contents to reveal layers below the masked layer.
~pages/Layers/aboutLayers.html
About layers
Layers let you organise your drawn objects more efficiently.
~pages/Layers/adjustmentLayers.html
Using adjustment layers
Adjustment layers make non-destructive corrections and enhancements to your layers.
~pages/Layers/createLayers.html
Create layers
Create new layers to help organise and manage your design.
~pages/Layers/layerBlendModes.html
Layer blending
Discussion of how layers can be blended together using the controls on the Layers panel.
~pages/Layers/layerBlendRanges.html
Layer blend ranges
Blend ranges specify the range of colours on a current layer which are blended with the underlying layer(s).
~pages/Layers/layerClip.html
Layer clipping
Clipping involves masking part of an object by placing it inside another object.
~pages/Layers/layerColours.html
Layer colours
Use layer colours to change the UI display colour of all object's path, nodes and handles within a chosen layer.
~pages/Layers/layerDropZones.html
Layer drop zones
Drop zones will highlight new layer positions when moving objects and layers.
~pages/Layers/layerImage.html
Image layers
Placed images will automatically be added to the Layers panel as an image layer.
~pages/Layers/layerOpacity.html
Layer opacity
The opacity of any layer can be changed in the Layers panel.
~pages/Layers/manageLayers.html
